{
  "name": "building-training-visual",
  "description": "Visual check of training buildings: driving center, blasting academy, management office, and geology lab",
  "steps": [
    {
      "command": "new_game seed:42 cash:150000",
      "timeout": 30,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "new_game seed:42 cash:150000"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 150000,
          "buildingCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "employee hire role:driller",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "ensurePanel",
          "panel": "employees"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driller\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driller\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -1000
        },
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 1
        }
      },
      "description": "Hired ahead of the orders below rather than after them (#556): a build order is queued work now, so the sites need someone on the roster to walk over and build them. Keeping this file’s own hires as the builders — rather than reaching for staffed:true — is what leaves the roster and proficiency counts it asserts where they were. Opens the Crew panel with ensurePanel rather than a bare toolbar click (#556): the toolbar tab toggles, so when a preceding step has already opened the panel a second click closes it and the hire button underneath reports zero size."
    },
    {
      "command": "employee hire role:blaster",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"blaster\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"blaster\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -1500
        },
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 2
        }
      },
      "description": "Hired ahead of the orders below rather than after them (#556): a build order is queued work now, so the sites need someone on the roster to walk over and build them. Keeping this file’s own hires as the builders — rather than reaching for staffed:true — is what leaves the roster and proficiency counts it asserts where they were."
    },
    {
      "command": "build driving_center at:3,5",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"build\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"driving_center\"] .bs-build-buy-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 3,
          "z": 5
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -12000
        },
        "equals": {
          "orderedBuildingCount": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "build blasting_academy at:10,3",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"blasting_academy\"] .bs-build-buy-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 10,
          "z": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -15000
        },
        "equals": {
          "orderedBuildingCount": 2
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "build management_office at:14,5",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"management_office\"] .bs-build-buy-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 14,
          "z": 5
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -8000
        },
        "equals": {
          "orderedBuildingCount": 3
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "build geology_lab at:20,5",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"geology_lab\"] .bs-build-buy-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 20,
          "z": 5
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -12000
        },
        "note": "Confirming placement only queues a construction site (#556) — the next step waits for all four orders above to actually land before anything below refers to a building by id."
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "wait_until field:buildingCount equals:4 max_ticks:400",
      "description": "Drive all four school/office sites to completion (#556).",
      "timeout": 125,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitUntil",
          "field": "buildingCount",
          "equals": 4,
          "maxTicks": 400,
          "timeoutMs": 120000
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 4,
          "orderedBuildingCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "build list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "build list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "employee list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "employee train 1 skill:driving.excavator building:1",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "ensurePanel",
          "panel": "employees"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-employee-id=\"1\"] .bs-detail-toggle"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-employee-id=\"1\"] .bs-train-btn[data-skill=\"driving.excavator\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-employee-id=\"1\"] .bs-train-btn[data-skill=\"driving.excavator\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -2500
        },
        "equals": {
          "trainingCount": 0
        }
      },
      "description": "Opens the Crew panel first (#556): the two hires moved to the top of the file so there is someone to build the schools, and the build steps between them and this one leave the Build panel showing — the employee row this clicks is not on screen without it. (#1203) Enrolment sends the employee walking to the school rather than relocating them instantly — trainingCount (trainingState !== null) stays 0 until they actually arrive and enter the building; the screenshot here is taken while they are still walking, mesh visible."
    },
    {
      "command": "employee list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "wait_until field:trainingCount equals:1 max_ticks:300",
      "description": "(#1203) Replaces a fixed `tick <N>` pad that assumed instant relocation: the walk to the school takes an unknown number of ticks depending on distance, so this waits for actual arrival (trainingState promoted from pendingTrainingState once the employee enters the building) rather than guessing.",
      "timeout": 90,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitUntil",
          "field": "trainingCount",
          "equals": 1,
          "maxTicks": 300,
          "timeoutMs": 60000
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "trainingCount": 1
        },
        "note": "The employee has walked to and entered the school — mesh hidden, course now ticking. Screenshot taken right after arrival."
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "employee list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 5",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "tick 5"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "trainingCount": 1
        },
        "note": "training takes 20 ticks from arrival — still in progress 5 ticks in"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "event choose 0",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "resolveEventIfPending"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Ordering the four buildings is queued construction now (#556), so the crew spends build ticks before the training block and a random event can fall due inside it — an unresolved event halts the very next `tick`. Resolved through the event dialog’s own buttons; whether an event is pending is decided from game state, not from whether the modal has rendered.",
      "role": "player",
      "commandOutcome": "either"
    },
    {
      "command": "wait_until field:trainingCount equals:0 max_ticks:300",
      "description": "(#1203) Replaces a fixed `tick <N>` pad for course completion — the exact tick the 20-tick course (from arrival, not from the `employee train` command) lands is no longer a fixed offset since arrival itself now takes a variable number of walk ticks.",
      "timeout": 90,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitUntil",
          "field": "trainingCount",
          "equals": 0,
          "maxTicks": 300,
          "timeoutMs": 60000
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "trainingCount": 0,
          "proficiencyTotal": 3
        },
        "note": "Course complete — driving.excavator gained (proficiencyTotal 2→3), training slot freed, employee left the building back onto its ring. Screenshot taken right after they reappear outside."
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "employee list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "state full",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "state full"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    }
  ],
  "shots": [
    {
      "name": "overview",
      "yaw": 0,
      "pitch": 45
    },
    {
      "name": "training-area",
      "yaw": 90,
      "pitch": 10
    },
    {
      "name": "closeup",
      "yaw": 45,
      "pitch": 30
    }
  ]
}
